    "paragraphs": [
      "President Trump and China's leader, X, ended a summit in Beijing on Friday without announcing any clear resolutions on major issues like TW, trade barriers and the war in Iran.",
      "Speaking to journalists aboard Air Force One after his departure, Mr. Trump said that he and Mr. X had talked \"in great detail\" about a long-delayed U.S. arms sale to TW, which China strongly opposes. The president said they had not discussed tariffs and he had not asked Mr. X \"for any favors\" in resolving the stalemate with Iran over the Strait of Hormuz.",
      "Earlier on Friday the two leaders had emphasized stability and friendly ties. Sitting beside Mr. X during a meeting at Zhongnanhai, the walled headquarters for China's ruling Communist Party, Mr. Trump said that the Chinese leader had \"become really a friend\" and that they felt similarly about the war in the Middle East. \"We've settled a lot of different problems that other people wouldn't have been able to settle,\" Mr. Trump said, without elaborating.",
      "For his part, Mr. X avoided wading into specific issues, a sharp contrast to a blunt warning over TW he issued on Thursday. He described the visit as a \"historic and symbolic\" milestone.",
      "\"We have established a new bilateral relationship, based on constructive strategic stability,\" he said.",
      "Mr. Trump told reporters on Air Force One that the two leaders had \"talked a lot about TW\" and a $14 billion weapons deal that the Trump administration has held off on approving to avoid upsetting China.",
      "\"I'll be making decisions,\" he said of the deal, without setting out a clear timeline. \"But you know, I think the last thing we need right now is a war that's 9,500 miles away.\"",
      "The Chinese government, which has not ruled out the use of force to take over TW, bristles at any American arms sales to the island. TW considers them essential for ensuring its defense against a Chinese invasion. Since 1979, TW has received American arms worth tens of billions of dollars, although much of this arsenal is now aged.",
      "The Trump-X summit was the first U.S. presidential visit to China in nearly a decade and was a test of whether the détente between the two nations would continue. It was heavy on public praise and pleasantries. At a lavish state banquet on Thursday evening, Mr. Trump invited Mr. X to visit the White House in September.",
      "Boeing Order: Mr. Trump told Fox News that Mr. X had agreed to order 200 airplanes from Boeing. He later repeated that to reporters on Air Force One, adding that there was \"a promise\" to buy 750 planes \"if they do a good job with the 200.\" Neither Boeing nor the Chinese have confirmed an agreement.",
      "Artificial Intelligence: Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said that the United States and China would discuss guardrails on A.I., including establishing a protocol for keeping powerful A.I. models out of the hands of nonstate actors.",
      "State media cast Trump's visit as a sign of China's rising stature.",
      "The summit's first day produced telling moments about the two leaders.",
      "Thursday's meeting in Beijing between President Trump and China's leader, X, took place mostly behind closed doors. Still, the first day of the summit between the leaders of the two most powerful countries produced some revelatory moments about each of the men, their leadership styles and their motivations as they navigate the world's most significant geopolitical rivalry.",
      "Here are some moments that stood out during the summit, which took place at the Great Hall of the People:",
      "Mr. X welcomed the American president with a grand parade, featuring both the Chinese military and a crowd of cheering children, some holding bouquets and American flags. At one point, Mr. Trump stopped to applaud the children.",
      "\"That was an honor like few I've ever seen before,\" Mr. Trump said. \"And I think I was particularly impressed by those children. They were happy. They were beautiful. The military is obvious. It couldn't be better. But those children were amazing.\"",
      "The opening remarks of each president revealed much about their personal styles. Mr. X adopted an almost philosophical tone about the role of great nations on the global stage and Mr. Trump employed his signature style of flattery and exaggeration.",
      "Speaking in Chinese, Mr. X cautioned against the \"Thucydides Trap\"—a concept rooted in the ancient rivalry between Athens and Sparta, which suggests that an established world power tends to be threatened by a rising one, leading to a clash. Mr. X urged Mr. Trump and the United States to avoid the mind-set that led the ancient Greek city-states to war.",
      "\"As the once-in-a-century transformation accelerates and the international landscape undergoes change and turmoil, the world has reached a new crossroads,\" Mr. X said. \"Can China and the United States overcome the 'Thucydides Trap' and establish a new paradigm for relations between great powers?\"",
      "For his turn, Mr. Trump boasted of the long relationship he has had with Mr. X, and the ease with which he persuaded top business executives to join the visit.",
      "\"There are those that say this is maybe the biggest summit ever,\" Mr. Trump said. \"They can never remember anything like it.\"",
      "Many observers closely watched how the two leaders would approach the issue of TW, which Beijing claims as part of its territory.",
      "Mr. X made clear that if the United States sided too heavily with TW, it could bring Beijing and Washington into conflict.",
      "Xinhua, China's official news agency, released a readout of the meeting, which included Mr. X's warning to Mr. Trump on the matter: \"Handled well, the two countries can maintain stability. If handled poorly, the two countries will collide or even clash, putting the entire U.S.-China relationship in an extremely dangerous situation,\" he said. Afterward, Mr. Trump was mum when asked by reporters about TW.",
      "\"We asked the top 30 in the world,\" Mr. Trump told the Chinese leader. \"Every single one of them said yes, and I didn't want the second or the third in the company. I wanted only the top. And they're here today to pay respects to you, to China, and they look forward to trade and good business.\""
    ],
