    "folder": "0610 AI 创业九死一生，连锁加盟稳赚不赔？",
    "titleZh": "AI 创业九死一生，连锁加盟稳赚不赔？",
    "title": "Why the World Needs More Franchises",
    "topicEn": "Technology",
    "topicZh": "科技",
    "byline": "The Economist, Published May 28, 2026",
    "paragraphs": [
      "How do you get rich in today's America? Founding an artificial-intelligence startup may look tempting, but most fail. Getting an advanced",
      "a reliable path to wealth, but now looks threatened by ai. Perhaps you should look instead to the company that has plausibly created more millionaires than any other in history: McDonald's. Most of its outlets are franchises, run by independent firms that pay royalties to the brand—and often make a fortune. If fast food isn't your thing, do not fear: the franchising model can be found everywhere from hotels to Pilates studios.",
      "They may not have the social cachet of a Wall Street corner office, but franchises make many Americans wealthy. If reports are to be believed, the country has even recently minted its first billionaire franchisee. They also boost growth. More countries should try creating a franchise economy—and America should protect the one it has from overregulation.",
      "Franchising works because of the deep laws of economics: it productively aligns incentives and divides labour. It crops up when a business requires a lot of employees to be geographically dispersed; when monitoring staff would be hard or expensive; and when knowledge of how local markets work is important. In such conditions it makes sense to divide responsibility between a franchisor, who focuses on the brand and the product, and a franchisee, who adapts to local conditions.",
      "The rest of the world can learn from the success of this model. Franchises thrive in part because of the strengths of American capitalism. Strong intellectual-property rights protect franchise brands, while deep capital markets make it easy for franchisees to borrow.",
      "But franchises have also benefited from good regulation. A vast amount of public information exists about how franchise models work. That is because franchisors must disclose how they make money from franchisees, provide estimates of startup costs and ongoing fees, and reveal any legal issues they are facing. Many also disclose in detail the financial performance of existing franchisees. Franchising flourished after rules mandating transparent disclosure were introduced in 1979. Since 1986 the number of franchise outlets has almost tripled.",
      "More recent attempts to regulate franchising have been less wise. Critics say franchising exploits and evades America's weak labour protections, for example by making it difficult for workers to unionise. Such critics would make franchisors joint employers of franchisee workers. That would expose franchisors to huge legal risk: they could, for example, be sued if a franchisee, who hires and pays staff, failed to pay overtime correctly. Such a shift would make franchising much riskier and, by centralising the system, undermine many of its advantages. It would ultimately be counterproductive for workers, who benefit from the many job opportunities franchises create, in industries mostly untouched by ai. Franchising may not be glamorous, but it is efficient. Best to keep it that way."
    ],
    "paragraphTranslations": [
      "为何世界需要更多特许经营 如今在美国，怎样才能赚到钱？创办一家人工智能初创公司看似很有吸引力，但大多数都会失败。攻读高等学历，再埋头打拼成 为企业律师或金融从业者，这条路曾是稳妥的致富途径，如今却受到人工智能的冲击。或许你可以把目光转向一家企业，它造就——的百万富翁数量据称超过了历史上任何其他公司 麦当劳。",
      "麦当劳的门店大多采用特许经营模式，由独立经营者运营，经营者 向品牌方缴纳加盟费，而且往往能赚得丰厚利润。如果你对快餐行业不感兴趣也没关系，从酒店到普拉提工作室，特许经营模式 随处可见。从事特许经营或许不如在华尔街办公室工作那样有社会声望，但它让很多美国人实现了财富增长。据相关报道，美国近期甚至出 现了首位特许经营领域的亿万富翁。",
      "特许经营还能推动经济增长。更多国家应当尝试发展特许经营经济，而美国也应避免过度监管，守护好现有的特许经营体系。特许经营能够发展壮大，源于基本的经济规律：它有效协调各方利益，实现分工协作。当企业需要大量员工分布在不同地区、监 管员工难度大且成本高，同时又需要经营者熟悉本地市场时，特许经营模式就会应运而生。",
      "在这种情况下，权责划分十分合理：特许方专注于品牌与产品，加盟商则根据当地实际情况开展经营。其他国家可以借鉴这一成功模式。特许经营蓬勃发展，部分得益于美国资本主义的优势。完善的知识产权体系为特许品牌提供保护，成熟的资本市场也让加盟商能够顺利获得贷款。合理的监管同样助力了特许经营的发展。特许经营的运作模式有大量公开信息可查。",
      "这是因为特许方必须公示其从加盟商处获利 的方式、启动资金与日常运营成本，并披露自身涉及的法律问题。不少特许方还会详细公布现有加盟商的经营收入情况。年，强制信息公开的相关规定正式实施，此后特许经营行业迎来快速发展。自 年以来，特许经营门店数量几乎增长了三倍。但近期出台的一些监管举措却并不妥当。批评者认为，特许经营利用了美国劳工保护制度的漏洞，甚至刻意规避相关规定，比如，使员工难以组建工会。",
      "有些批评者主张，让品牌特许方与加盟商共同承担雇主责任。这会让特许方面临巨大的法律风险：举例来说，员工由加盟商招聘并发放薪酬，一旦加盟商未按规定支付加班费，特许方也可能遭到起诉。监管规则一旦做出这样的调整，特许 经营的经营风险会大幅上升，经营模式走向集中化，其原有的诸多优势也会消失。对从业者来说，这么做到头来只会得不偿失。",
      "这些行业基本未受人工智能影响，从业者也得益于特许经营带来的众多工作岗位。特许经营或许并不光鲜，却具备很高的运转效率。最好维持现状。"
    ],
