    "exerciseText": "1.\n根据英文释义写出文中出现的对应单词\n_________: criticizing popular beliefs or established customs and ideas\n_________: to refuse to accept something or someone as true, good, or reasonable\n2.\n一词多义\nWhich of the following uses of the underlined word is CLOSEST in meaning to the one in the\nsentence \"Mr. Isherwood stares at his younger lover with a kind of predatory intensity, while\nelsewhere a collector stands sculpture-stiff in a business suit with fists clenched, near his\npink-robed wife, whose snarling smile is echoed, cartoon-fashion, in the faces carved on a\nNative American totem pole planted nearby.\" ____\nA. The company is facing stiff competition from online retailers worldwide.\nB. If you don't pay your taxes on time, you will face stiff penalties.\nC. Her legs were stiff and sore after walking around the sprawling museum all day.\nD. Travelers are complaining about the stiff hotel rates in Paris during the retrospective\nexhibition.\n3.\n根据给定中文回译英文\n英国艺术家大卫·霍克尼于周四在伦敦家中去世，享年 88 岁。自 20 世纪 50 年代末和 60 年代初起，\n在抽象艺术主导数十年之后，他凭借布局精妙、色彩典雅的绘画作品，将英美艺术界的瞩目焦点重\n新引向具象艺术与叙事艺术。\n_____________________________________________________________________________________\n_____________________________________________________________________________________",
