    "exerciseText": "1.\n根据英文释义写出文中出现的对应单词或词组\n______: to confuse sb. completely; to be too difficult or strange for sb. to understand or explain\n______: (of a rate of increase) becoming faster and faster\n2.\n一词多义\nWhich of the following underlined phrases is closest in meaning to the one in the sentence \"You search\nand brainstorm and then, as if by magic, one day the answer pops into your mind, and at this point, the\nlearning curve turns exponential. Some people hate the stress stirred up by that situation, but it's what\nmental marathoners live for.\"? ____\nA. His comments stirred up resentment among local residents.\nB. His fiery words stirred the supporters up for the coming protest.\nC. We've got enough problems without you trying to stir things up.\nD. They saw first a cloud of dust and then the car that was stirring it up.\n3.\n翻译：根据给定中文回译英文\n在这个时代，文字、歌曲、电影都越来越多地由已有作品整合生成，文化产出会让人愈发似曾相识。\nAI\n与之相反，心智长跑者想要创作出带有个人烙印、映照独特自我的作品。他们会想方设法利用\n来增强自身的主观能动性，而非削弱它。\n_____________________________________________________________________________________\n_________________________________________________________________________",
